{"uid":"4ae70d0acee5466c","name":"test_the_fresh_episode_survives_a_whitespace_edged_minted_key","fullName":"tests.test_confirmed_petition_survives_archive_and_episode#test_the_fresh_episode_survives_a_whitespace_edged_minted_key","historyId":"09d77b2801a2e7b342dcb09599887515","time":{"start":1791980731109,"stop":1791980731115,"duration":6},"description":"Regression (found by this task's own validation, which saw this\n    module exit nonzero once): the exclusion has to survive the episode\n    boundary for EVERY key `secrets.token_bytes(32)` can mint, not for 95%\n    of them. The store used to hold the key as raw bytes and read it back\n    through `.strip()`, so a key whose first or last byte was an ASCII\n    whitespace byte came back short, the rebuilt authority's keyed MAC\n    mismatched, and approach 1's own CONFIRMED obligation was read as\n    tampered/empty -- i.e. re-litigated by approach 2, the exact failure\n    requirement C.4 forbids. The key is hex encoded in the store now\n    (`petitions._decode_key_material`); the minted key here is pinned to\n    the worst case (leading `\\n`, trailing `\\t`) so the check is\n    deterministic rather than a ~1-in-22 flake.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Regression (found by this task's own validation, which saw this<br />\nmodule exit nonzero once): the exclusion has to survive the episode<br />\nboundary for EVERY key <code>secrets.token_bytes(32)</code> can mint, not for 95%<br />\nof them. The store used to hold the key as raw bytes and read it back<br />\nthrough <code>.strip()</code>, so a key whose first or last byte was an ASCII<br />\nwhitespace byte came back short, the rebuilt authority's keyed MAC<br />\nmismatched, and approach 1's own CONFIRMED obligation was read as<br />\ntampered/empty -- i.e. re-litigated by approach 2, the exact failure<br />\nrequirement C.4 forbids. The key is hex encoded in the store now<br />\n(<code>petitions._decode_key_material</code>); the minted key here is pinned to<br />\nth